# Regenerate the artefact commit stamp (paper subtitle) before each build.
# The file defines \artefactshavalue, loaded at preamble level by belief.tex.
# Perl q[...] (no interpolation) is load-bearing: in a double-quoted string
# Perl interpolates "$(" as its group-id list variable, which is exactly the
# mangled-subtitle bug this line replaces (caught by Matthew, 2026-11-01).
system(q[printf '%s%s%s' '\newcommand{\artefactshavalue}{' "$(git rev-parse --short=10 HEAD)" '}' > commitsha.tex]) == 0
  or warn "commitsha.tex not regenerated (git unavailable?)\n";
